-- Prove2me | Definitions.Def_MasulloRH_HeightTwoEnergyTable
-- name    : MasulloRH_HeightTwoEnergyTable
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @sflicht
-- created : 2026-11-21T19:54:32.703358+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/b90d114d-6b75-402e-9915-d52f1b450b4e
-- title:
--   Rational partition and candidate cell-energy bounds for the height-two theta witness
-- statement:
--   This definition records the exact rational data for a finite numerical certificate for the height-two theta witness. It supplies endpoints $u_0,\ldots,u_{455}$ and rational numbers $A_0,\ldots,A_{454}$, intended as candidate bounds for the weighted energy on the cells $[u_i,u_{i+1}]$.
--
--   The associated residual is the actual canonical function $r(x)=p_2(x)-\sum_{j=0}^{10}a_j\theta(x-y_j)$, with coefficients and shifts from `MasulloRH_HeightTwoWitness`. The intended cell inequality is
--
--   $$\int_{u_i}^{u_{i+1}}e^{3x/2+11|x|/24}|r(x)|^2\,dx\le A_i.$$
--
--   The two arrays contain only rational numbers. This definition does not assert the displayed inequality, integrability, an error bound, or the final whole-line estimate. Those are separate proof obligations. The endpoint and budget arithmetic are also kept in separately checked proofs.
-- source:
--   Exact rational candidate table generated for the Prove2Me Masullo RH specialization mission from the eleven-term height-two witness. The supporting exterior theorem is https://prove2.me/theorems/64eea16b-a1b5-4d72-9c75-6b61b57ddea4 . This is a new numerical certificate construction, not a table quoted from the Masullo manuscript. Data source and generation digests are retained in the contribution archive.

import Mathlib

/-!
# Rational partition data for the height-two theta residual

The table contains a contiguous candidate partition of [-4,4] and candidate
upper bounds for its weighted cell integrals.  These definitions assert no
analytic inequality; the actual canonical integral bounds and the total
budget must be proved separately.
-/

